  "query_preview": "the SCA for the coastal waters through Sunday morning \ndue to a continuation of the 5 ft seas. Additional SCAs are \nlikely to be issued for the lower bay late tonight as another \nsurge in winds drops across the local waters, but will hold off \non extending the ongoing headlines due to the relative lull in \nwinds this afternoon and evening. \n\nHigh pressure situates south of the area Sunday and winds \nshould shift to the W by Sunday afternoon and then SW by the \nevening hours. Winds speeds also diminish with sub-SCA \nconditions by the afternoon as well. Additional periods of \nelevated winds are possible again Sunday night (in SW flow) and \nthen Monday morning-afternoon (in W-NW flow) behind another cold\nfront. SCAs are again possible. Sub- SCA/generally benign \nconditions return Tuesday through Thursday. A stronger system \ncould affect the waters late next week, but overall confidence \nis low.",
